{"id": "21164", "revid": "1822", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=21164", "title": "Mangan", "text": "Mangan is the capital of North Sikkim.\nUnderstand.\nThe sleepy town of Mangan happens to be the district headquarters of North Sikkim. It is also the gateway to the northern towns of Sikkim, places like Yumthang, Katao, Chungthang, Lachung and Lachen. Mangan is also 10 km from Dzongu, which is reserved from the Lepcha aboriginal people of Sikkim.\nGet in.\nMangan can be reached from Siliguri by passing through Rangpo, Singtham, Dikchu and Makha. In fact, the town lies in the route which connects Gangtok with the extreme northern towns of Sikkim, like Lachen, and Lachung.\nJeeps are available from Siliguri to Mangan.\nMangan can also be from Gangtok. Shared jeeps and taxis are available."}
{"id": "21165", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=21165", "title": "Mangaratiba", "text": "Mangaratiba is a municipality in the state of Rio de Janeiro. For tourists, it is both a place to catch a ship to Ilha Grande and the site of some of the most beautiful and traditional beaches in the state.\nGet in.\nBy bus from Rio de Janeiro or by car by the road BR-101.\nFrom the Rio's Central Zone, there are buses available in the long-distance bus station that go directly from the downtown area of Rio de Janeiro to Mangaratiba. This route is made by the bus company \"Costa Verde\". Mangaratiba is about 100 km from downtown Rio.\nAlthough there are no urban public transport lines connecting directly Mangaratiba to the Rio's Central Zone, there are urban bus lines that connect Mangaratiba to peripheral places of the metropolitan area of Rio de Janeiro, such as the municipalities of Duque de Caxias, Nova Igua\u00e7u and Itagua\u00ed.\nGo next.\nNote: You can easily rent a place to park your car in Mangaratiba."}
